    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0144" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    UNA Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Special Assistant to the Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pasvolsky</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d83-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-12-22">December 22, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Voting in the Security Council</p>
                <p>I reported orally to the President on the latest developments on this matter and
                    indicated to him that we were doing what we could <pb facs="0145" n="63"
                        xml:id="pg63"/> to press the Russians and British for an early decision. I
                    told him that if we received “yes” that we hoped to send out invitations for a
                    March meeting. He felt that would be entirely appropriate.</p>
                <p>He indicated some displeasure at the fact that things were moving so slowly in
                    this field.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        E. R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius,
                                Jr.</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush">cc: Mr. Edwin
                            Wilson
                    </p>
                    <p>Mr. Alger Hiss
                    </p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
